A||N||6||shelfran||Door was closed hard and now I can't open it||||1||
Z||000000||shelfran||07-10-2001||11:47 PM||||My son slammed the drivers door on my 84 Fiero and now I can't get it open. Before I destroy the door getting it off, does anyone have a suggestion, or has anyone ever had this problem? I tried a door opener tool in case the lock pivot was just "locked" and it didn't do any good. Someone please let me know.  Thanks....Frank Sheldon...PS...Is there anyone in the Albany NY area that uses this Fiero Forum?  shelfran@hotmail.com||||reg||1
Z||000001||StuGood||07-11-2001||10:07 AM||||So, what's the problem?  You've got the other door, right? Just use that one.  BTW, make sure son doesn't slam <B>that</B> door  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Alternatively, use passenger door to get in, crank down the driver's door window, leave it rolled down, and you can play "Dukes of Hazzard," jumping in and out the door window  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Okay, that wasn't very nice.  'Fit were me, I guess I'd get in the passenger door, remove the seats, and work on getting the driver's inside door panel off.  From that point, I'd see what's wrong inside.  Several recent posts discussed door latch/lock problems (clips falling off, etc.), so a search might provide you with some ideas.<P>That's all I can offer.  Good luck  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">      ||||reg||12
Z||000002||stsmithgt||07-11-2001||10:22 AM||||I'd lift the handle trying to feel if it is operating anything.  If it is, the part about taking the panel off checking to see if the inside components are good.  After that, I would change to german know how.  I'd have someone hold the handle up and kick the crap out of the door until it opened.( or something like that.)   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||07-11-2001||11:46 AM||||he prob just knocked off one of the rod linkages. should still open from inside. If it wont, try taking off the inside armrest to gain some access to the inside. then use a small flashlite and screwdriver to trip the lock from inside. If I remember theres a few pretty good size access holes under the armrest. If not you can make one if your careful, the armrest will cover it up when its back on.||||reg||1
Z||000004||starfighter007@msn.com||07-11-2001||03:30 PM||||Try pushing on the door from the outside while lifting the handle.that is of course that none of the rods fell of on the inside of the door.my gut feeling is that the way you described what had happened ,that a rod came off the locking mech.I am now wondering that maybe if you went to a body shop maybe the can open it from the outside for you .The more I think about it that is what I would do first.goodluck||||reg||1
Z||000005||qwikgta||07-11-2001||09:55 PM||||A similar thing happened to me the other day.  Some of the posts from a few months back were mine.  They have some great pics with them.  I also agree that it sounds like one of the "rods" was shaken loose.  I also had to remove the interor door panel with the door shut, it was a ***** .  I wasted all the little clips doing it because with the door shut you have no room to remove the panel.  It can be done but you have to go slow and expect to do some damage.  I did not have to remove the seats but MAYBE it would have made a diff.  Once the panel is off you can get in there with a flashlight and look around, it should be a no brainer by then.  Good luck<P>Rob<P>------------------<BR>qwikgta@yahoo.com<BR>88 T-Top coupe, 65K, Header no Cat, 16" GTZ rims, short shifter, swaybar, open element air cleaner, hood vents.<BR>http://robsfieroproject.homestead.com/index.html<BR>http://vafiero.com<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||shelfran||07-12-2001||06:35 PM||||Thanks for the suggestion. I will try to remove the seat for more room to work. I have 5 Fiero's..84,85,86,87,88, and I am building a Kit Car on the 84. Your picture of the Fiero was pretty good.<P>Take care,<P>Frank Sheldon    shelfran@hotmail.com<p>[This message has been edited by shelfran (edited 07-12-2001).]||||reg||14
